-- ============================================================================
-- 33: render-replica LIVE — render-field gaps closed/confirmed (2026-06-14).
-- JOB1 hit-flash/super-aura MECHANISM verdict + JOB2 three small wire gaps
-- (infinite-time / battle-state / per-side win count). Branch feat/render-replica-live.
-- Grounded in marvelous2 bank03/bank1a/bank0f + pl_mem.asm/work.asm + live Oracle
-- (prod 149.28.44.118, MAPLECAST_ORACLE_PROBE, READ-ONLY).
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

-- ---- sources ----
UPSERT source:hitflash_palette_chain SET kind='code',
  ref='_marv_re/build/bank03.asm loc_8c035162 (11.. ) + loc_8c035000 (11891 "happens on hit") + bank1a.asm loc_8c1A8092 (0xA05F9000 PALETTE_RAM upload) + bank04.asm loc_8c0442cc lit-pool',
  note='HIT-FLASH / HURT-RECOLOR is a PALETTE rebuild, not an overlay quad. CHAIN: per-char render setup loc_8c0442cc loads the helper ptr bank03.loc_8c035162 (lit pool @bank04.asm:9959 next to load-anim loc_8c034e8c). loc_8c035162 reads char+0x12e (offset literal loc_8c035250 #data 0x012e) as the HURT-EFFECT-TYPE selector (u16 into r14), dispatches cmp/eq on 0..0x0A, and via bsr loc_8c035000 ("happens on hit") rebuilds the 16-entry palette into a work-RAM staging buffer (loops mov.w r3,@r7 at r14+0x10; base table bank13.loc_8c1355d4, GameGlobalPointer-relative). loc_8c035000 reads char+0x25 (pl_palid_match), char+0x164 (Dat_Pal ptr), char+0x1 (char_id, for per-char special-case banks 0x01/0x22/0x37/0x14), and the "Palette Offset" 0x0300. The VBlank/display bank1a routine (loc_8c1A8092 region) then copies the staging buffers into PVR PALETTE_RAM at 0xA05F9000 (loc_8c1A80Dc #data 0xA05F9000), gated by dirty flags (tst 0x01/0x02/0x04). Body sprites are PVR-PALETTIZED textures that SAMPLE PALETTE_RAM (proven: finding:replica_live_palette_gap = a body renders BLACK when its PALETTE_RAM bank is zero). So a hurt-flash recolor flows char+0x12e -> staging -> PALETTE_RAM -> body re-samples.';

UPSERT source:replica_live_fieldgap_addrs SET kind='code',
  ref='_marv_re/memory/work.asm:9,20-24 + pl_mem.asm:301-304 + live Oracle prod 149.28.44.118',
  note='CONFIRMED ADDRESSES. (1) GAME MODE block 0x8C26828C (work.asm:22) = the time-mode/match-mode selector; reached via GameGlobalPointer(0x8C26823C)->0x8C268240 + 0x4C. Oracle live read 0x8C268288..: 00 01 FF 00 | 02 03 06 01 (so 0x28C=0x02 mode, 0x28E=0x06 frameskip "FreeSelectNormal=6"), 0x291=0x01 stage-unlocks. INFINITE-TIME OBSERVABLE: in_match(0x8C289624)=1 yet timer(0x8C289630)=0x63=99 frozen + both chars HP=144 = infinite/idle match. (2) BATTLE STATE 0x8C2895F0 (work.asm:9) Oracle live = 0x04 (in-round); count array 0x8C2895E0 cycles 0x03->0x04 across transitions. (3) PER-SIDE WIN COUNT = char+0x540 num_wins (pl_mem.asm:301; +0x541 num_lose, +0x542 num_draw, +0x543 handicap_level). Oracle live P1C1+0x540=00 wins, +0x543=02 handicap (the 0x02 is HANDICAP, not a win). 0x540<stride 0x5A4 -> already inside the shipped char_str region.';

-- ---- JOB1 verdict ----
UPSERT finding:replica_live_hitflash_verdict SET
  statement='VERDICT: MVC2 hit-flash / hurt-recolor is a PALETTE SWAP into PVR PALETTE_RAM, i.e. ALREADY CAPTURED FOR FREE by the render-replica on-change PVR-palette tail (pvrPalSig folds the full 4KB PALETTE_RAM 0x1000..0x1FFF) — NOT genuinely-unrendered client work and NOT a separate cat 1..4 effect-pool overlay quad. CODE CHAIN (source:hitflash_palette_chain): per-char render setup loc_8c0442cc -> loc_8c035162 reads char+0x12e (hurt-effect-type) -> dispatch -> loc_8c035000 ("happens on hit") rebuilds the 16-color palette into work-RAM staging (reads char+0x25 palid, +0x164 Dat_Pal, +0x1 char_id) -> bank1a VBlank routine copies staging into PVR PALETTE_RAM 0xA05F9000 -> the palettized body sprite re-samples PALETTE_RAM. Because the body is a PVR-palettized texture (proven by finding:replica_live_palette_gap: zero bank => black body), the recolor IS in PALETTE_RAM, and the existing pvrPalSig on-change tail ships it whenever it changes. CONSEQUENCE: when a real hit lands, the hurt palette will change pvrPalSig => the 32KB pvr_regs tail re-ships => the client updatePalette() re-uploads => the body recolors with ZERO new client/wire work, PROVIDED the palette-fix on-change tail (finding:replica_live_palette_fix) is actually DEPLOYED. The reason replica bodies do not flash today is most likely that the palette-fix tail is built-not-deployed (the prefix-snapshot palette is frozen), NOT a missing mechanism. CAVEAT/RESIDUAL: a distinct ADDITIVE super-AURA (full-screen flash / character outline glow) may additionally be a cat 1..4 effect-pool node rendered by the faithful effect walker (RenderExtra char+0x151=0x01 baseline live) — that path is separate and already walked if the pool node exists; only the per-body HURT recolor is settled here as palette-swap. EMPIRICAL STATUS: the code chain is end-to-end CONFIRMED; the live PALETTE_RAM-changes-on-hit read could NOT be captured because (a) the prod match was idle/infinite-time the whole probe window (in_match=1, HP pinned 144, timer frozen 99, +0x12e constant 0x10/0x18) so no hit landed, and (b) the Oracle mem: probe cannot read PVR reg space (guest 0x005FA400 reads back all-zero — not main RAM). Confirm-on-hit deferred to a live combat window: probe char+0x12e transition vs a host-side pvrPalSig-changed log.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

-- ---- JOB2 gaps ----
UPSERT finding:replica_live_render_field_gaps SET
  statement='THREE small genuine wire gaps confirmed + shipped (server core/network/maplecast_replica_live.cpp buildTables, commit b3459e656). (1) INFINITE-TIME: ggp_acc region EXTENDED D(0x8C268240,0x40)->0x60 so it reaches the Game-mode block 0x8C26828C (work.asm:22), the time-mode selector; the client can then render the HUD timer as infinity instead of the held-99 heuristic. Infinite-time observable Oracle-confirmed: in_match=1 + timer 0x8C289630 frozen 0x63=99 + HP 144 both. (2) BATTLE-STATE: NEW region D(0x8C2895C0,0x60,"battle") covers Battle State 0x8C2895F0 (work.asm:9, round-intro/KO/win-screen transitions); Oracle live=0x04. (3) PER-SIDE WIN COUNT = char+0x540 num_wins (pl_mem.asm:301) — ALREADY inside the shipped char_str region (0x540<0x5A4), so NO new wire; documented in-line + client draws win stars from char[pointSlot]+0x540. Build: headless MAPLECAST_HEADLESS=ON on dev 65.109.77.178, binary md5 8a4566083e9aa93a2e9d8fc7fc4423c1 (26,203,648 B). DEPLOY STAGED, NOT yet live: prod binary md5 ad968c65c8d1775ce71b0efbeb32893d backed up to /usr/local/bin/flycast.bak-fieldgaps-PREDEPLOY-20260614; new binary staged at /usr/local/bin/flycast.staged-fieldgaps (md5 verified == dev build). The atomic swap+restart is USER-COORDINATED (a restart interrupts the live match) — swap: systemctl stop maplecast-headless && cp /usr/local/bin/flycast.staged-fieldgaps /usr/local/bin/flycast && systemctl start maplecast-headless; rollback: cp the .bak-fieldgaps-PREDEPLOY back. Wire cost: +0x20 (ggp_acc) +0x60 (battle) = +0x80 bytes/frame, zstd-trivial (stable). CLIENT (mvc2-sprite-render-expert, coordinating HUD tag-team bars): read game-mode 0x8C26828C for infinite-time, battle-state 0x8C2895F0 for round-phase overlays, char+0x540 for win stars.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

-- ---- edges ----
RELATE finding:replica_live_hitflash_verdict->cites->source:hitflash_palette_chain;
RELATE finding:replica_live_render_field_gaps->cites->source:replica_live_fieldgap_addrs;
